-- v2 -> v3: drop the `version` column.
--
-- Uploaded resources are now immutable — the engine no longer compares a content version, so a
-- COMPLETED row's mere existence is the proof of backup. Unlike 1.sqm this migration is
-- ROW-PRESERVING: existing rows (especially COMPLETED ones) MUST survive, because a surviving
-- COMPLETED row is exactly what stops the next discovery cycle from re-uploading an already-stored
-- resource. `ALTER TABLE … DROP COLUMN` is SQLite 3.35 grammar (see the dialect bump in
-- domain/engine/build.gradle.kts); both drivers execute it natively. Migration SQL is raw (no
-- `AS LedgerState`/`AS Instant` type annotations).
ALTER TABLE ledgerRow DROP COLUMN version;
